  "goodToKnow": "Jawohl is an emphatic yes, associated with the military (Jawohl, Herr Feldwebel!), so it can sound stiff or comical in everyday speech. Used ironically, it suggests mock obedience: Jawohl, Chef! It's also used to cheer enthusiastically, for example when your team scores. In normal conversation, Germans say Ja, genau, Klar or Na klar. Stressed on the second syllable: ya-VOHL."
